# Age of Mortals — feats (pp.50-51) and leeching (p.56).
Alternate Form (Age of Mortals)	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:General	DESC:You can take a humanoid or animal form, as some dragons can.	BENEFIT:Once a day, assume one specific humanoid or animal form of Medium size or smaller, as polymorph on yourself at your caster level, regaining no hit points; you may stay in it until you choose to return. Special: May be taken more than once; each adds one use per day (silver, gold and bronze dragons too).	PRETEXT:Dragon (adult or older), caster level 5th	SOURCEPAGE:p.50
Charming (Age of Mortals)	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:General	DESC:Others find your company appealing.	BENEFIT:+2 on Diplomacy and Bluff checks.	BONUS:SKILL|Diplomacy,Bluff|2	SOURCEPAGE:p.50
Discipline	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:General	DESC:You keep your composure under pressure.	BENEFIT:+1 on Will saves and +2 on Concentration checks.	BONUS:SAVE|Will|1	BONUS:SKILL|Concentration|2	SOURCEPAGE:p.50
Education (Age of Mortals)	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:General	DESC:You had years of formal schooling.	BENEFIT:All Knowledge skills are class skills for you. +1 on all checks with any two Knowledge skills of your choice. Special: Only at 1st level.	CSKILL:TYPE=Knowledge	SOURCEPAGE:p.50
Haggler (Age of Mortals)	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:General	DESC:You are skilled at business deals.	BENEFIT:+2 competence bonus on all Appraise and Bluff checks.	BONUS:SKILL|Appraise,Bluff|2|TYPE=Competence	SOURCEPAGE:p.50
Heroic Surge (Age of Mortals)	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:General	DESC:You draw on inner reserves to act more in a round.	BENEFIT:Take an additional move or attack action, before or after your regular actions, once per day for every four character levels you have attained; never more than once per round.	SOURCEPAGE:p.50
Horned Stampede	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:General	DESC:You charge with your horns lowered.	BENEFIT:Your horns deal 2d8 + 1-1/2 times your Strength bonus in a charge (normally 2d6 + 1-1/2 times your Strength bonus).	PRERACE:1,Minotaur	PRESTAT:1,STR=13	PREFEAT:1,Power Attack	PRETEXT:Minotaur, Strength 13, Power Attack	SOURCEPAGE:p.51
Improved Taunt (Age of Mortals)	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:General	DESC:You enrage others with insults and jeering.	BENEFIT:A Bluff check against the opponent's Sense Motive: -2 on its attack rolls and AC, and its attitude two steps more hostile (friendly to unfriendly, indifferent to hostile). Lasts 1 round plus your Charisma bonus, twice that if the Bluff beats the Sense Motive by 10 or more; once per encounter. Against a crowd: Bluff against DC 10 + 1 per two targets (10 people DC 15, 40 people DC 30) shifts their attitude one step worse. Special: Close friends and long-time acquaintances of the taunter gain a +4 familiarity bonus to resist if targeted.	PRESTAT:1,CHA=13	PRETEXT:Charisma 13, Taunt exceptional ability	SOURCEPAGE:p.51
Lucky (Age of Mortals)	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:General	DESC:You survive by sheer good fortune.	BENEFIT:+1 luck bonus on all saving throws.	BONUS:SAVE|ALL|1|TYPE=Luck	SOURCEPAGE:p.51
Mimic (Age of Mortals)	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:General	DESC:You have a natural talent for impersonation.	BENEFIT:+2 competence bonus on Disguise and Perform checks.	BONUS:SKILL|Disguise,TYPE.Perform|2|TYPE=Competence	SOURCEPAGE:p.51
Quick-Thinking (Age of Mortals)	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:General	DESC:You react quickly to danger.	BENEFIT:+2 on initiative and +2 on Spot checks.	BONUS:COMBAT|INITIATIVE|2	BONUS:SKILL|Spot|2	SOURCEPAGE:p.51
Sharp-Eyed (Age of Mortals)	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:General	DESC:You have an eye for small details.	BENEFIT:+2 competence bonus on Search and Sense Motive checks.	BONUS:SKILL|Search,Sense Motive|2|TYPE=Competence	SOURCEPAGE:p.51
Spellcasting Prodigy (Age of Mortals)	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:General	DESC:You have an exceptional gift for magic.	BENEFIT:For bonus spells and save DCs, treat your primary spellcasting ability (Wisdom for divine, Intelligence for arcane) as 2 points higher. With more than one spellcasting class it applies to only one. Special: Only at 1st level. Taken again (for example, as a human), it applies to another class. You may take it with no spellcasting class yet.	SOURCEPAGE:p.51
Street Smart (Age of Mortals)	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:General	DESC:You keep an ear to the ground.	BENEFIT:+2 on Bluff and Gather Information checks.	BONUS:SKILL|Bluff,Gather Information|2	SOURCEPAGE:p.51
Stubborn (Age of Mortals)	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:General	DESC:You are headstrong.	BENEFIT:+1 on Will saves and +2 on Intimidate checks.	BONUS:SAVE|Will|1	BONUS:SKILL|Intimidate|2	SOURCEPAGE:p.51
Trustworthy (Age of Mortals)	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:General	DESC:You project a friendly demeanor.	BENEFIT:+2 competence bonus on Diplomacy and Gather Information checks.	BONUS:SKILL|Diplomacy,Gather Information|2|TYPE=Competence	SOURCEPAGE:p.51
Leech Item	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:Metamagic	DESC:You draw a magic item's potential into your spells.	BENEFIT:Each point of an item's potential you drain raises your effective spellcasting level by one. As a move action that provokes no attack of opportunity, drain up to your primary casting ability modifier (Intelligence for wizards; Charisma for bards and sorcerers; Wisdom for clerics, druids, mystics and paladins) in a round; use it on a spell cast the next round or it is wasted. Your effective level can never exceed your spellcaster level + that modifier (a 4th-level wizard with Int 14 reaches 6th). Potential (Table 2-1): armor, shields and weapons 1 per 500 stl of value; potions 1 per 50 (destroyed); rings, rods and wondrous items 1 per 1,000; scrolls 1 per spell level (destroyed); staffs 1 per charge and wands 1 per 2 charges, rounded down (neither recharges unless it recharges itself); minor artifacts 5 per caster level; major artifacts at the DM's discretion. Intelligent items and major artifacts resist with a Will save (DC equal to Ego, or 20 + 1 per enhancement bonus + 5 per special ability). Items regain 1 point per 24 hours (not potions, scrolls, or most staffs and wands); one drained of a quarter of its potential stops working until fully recharged; one drained to 0 makes a Fortitude save (2 + half its caster level against DC 20) or becomes permanently nonmagical.	PRETEXT:Spellcaster level 3rd	SOURCEPAGE:p.56
Improved Leech Item	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:Metamagic	DESC:You drain more of an item's power.	BENEFIT:As a full-round action that provokes an attack of opportunity, drain up to your primary casting ability modifier + half your spellcaster level, rounded down (a 7th-level wizard with Int 14: 5); use it the next round or it is wasted. The same cap as Leech Item applies (7th-level, Int 14: 9th).	PREFEAT:1,Leech Item	PRETEXT:Spellcaster level 7th, Leech Item	SOURCEPAGE:p.56
Quick Leech	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:Metamagic	DESC:You leech in an instant.	BENEFIT:Leech as a free action (instead of Leech Item's move action) or a move action (instead of Improved Leech Item's full-round action), keeping only half the potential leeched.	PREFEAT:1,Leech Item	PRETEXT:Leech Item, spellcaster level 5th	SOURCEPAGE:p.56
